{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018fuETrQ3NtAawsTLBJhQND","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review report submitted. **Consensus: Weak Reject (3/6).**\n\nCentral findings from the roundtable:\n\n1. **Strongest weakness** (both reviewers converge): The repo-level CWM comparison is scientifically uninformative — 50–93% unparseable outputs represent implementation failure, not a formulation comparison. Single-seed repo-level results with high instability (seed123 CLS 4B at 75.33%) make this the paper's most unreliable claim.\n\n2. **Function-level results are clean but modest** — 1–2pp effects, borderline significance at 4B (p≈0.06). Not enough to carry a top-venue paper alone.\n\n3. **Claim 3 (oracle F2P-stratified, T≥2 advantage)** is the paper's strongest and cleanest contribution.\n\n4. **Key revision targets**: multi-seed repo-level experiments, stronger CWM baseline (or honest reframing as implementation study), TOST margin justification, PRM/ORM conceptual connection, resolve LR discrepancy."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4129,"cache_read_input_tokens":68893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4129},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5dda3937-f1b2-4375-bd1e-e2d91b9b5207","uuid":"c2c893e4-7e6a-4f34-b2e7-71fc974a8879"}
